- [ ] FPS display still works
- [ ] Unit tests: ProcessingRenderer with MockPApplet
- [ ] Integration test: Run application with ProcessingRenderer

### Technical Notes
- This is essentially extracting OnScreen.java's current logic into the interface
- Keep PApplet alive during this phase - we're not removing Processing yet
- Use this to validate the interface is sufficient
- Fix any missing methods in IRenderer interface as you discover them

### Implementation Pattern
```java
public class ProcessingRenderer implements IRenderer {
    private PApplet p;

    public ProcessingRenderer(PApplet pApplet) {
        this.p = pApplet;
    }

    @Override
    public void drawPoint(float x, float y, float z, int r, int g, int b) {
        p.stroke(r, g, b);
        p.point(x, y, z);
    }

    // ... etc
}
```

