## P0: Refactor OnScreen to Use IRenderer

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Medium (6-10 hours)
**Dependencies**: P0 Processing Renderer
**Spec Reference**: User requirements for incremental migration
**Status Reference**: STATUS-libgdx-migration.md (OnScreen.java 205 lines)

### Description
Refactor OnScreen.java to use IRenderer interface instead of calling PApplet methods directly. This proves we can decouple the visualization logic from the rendering backend.

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] OnScreen.java constructor takes IRenderer instead of PApplet
- [ ] All PApplet method calls replaced with IRenderer method calls
- [ ] No direct PApplet usage in OnScreen.java (except for constants like PI, if needed)
- [ ] Application runs with ProcessingRenderer with identical visual output
- [ ] All interactions work (mouse rotation, etc.)
- [ ] No regressions in frame rate or visual quality
- [ ] Code compiles and all tests pass

### Technical Notes
- This is mechanical refactoring, should be straightforward
- Keep careful notes on any Processing constants/utilities still needed
- May discover missing methods in IRenderer - add them
- Use find/replace carefully: `p.` → `renderer.`
- Test thoroughly after each batch of changes

### Before/After Example
```java
// BEFORE
private void drawAxes(float size) {
    p.strokeWeight(1);
    p.stroke(220, 0, 0);
    p.line(0, 0, 0, size, 0, 0);
}

// AFTER
private void drawAxes(float size) {
    renderer.setStrokeWeight(1);
    renderer.setStroke(220, 0, 0);
    renderer.drawLine(0, 0, 0, size, 0, 0);
}
```

