## P1: Application Lifecycle Migration (TesseractMain)

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Large (12-18 hours)
**Dependencies**: P1 LibGDX Renderer Foundation
**Spec Reference**: User requirements for ARM Mac support
**Status Reference**: STATUS-libgdx-migration.md (TesseractMain.java lifecycle section)

### Description
Migrate TesseractMain from extending PApplet to implementing LibGDX ApplicationListener. This removes the JOGL dependency entirely by switching to LibGDX's LWJGL3 backend for window/OpenGL context management.

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] TesseractMain implements ApplicationListener (not extends PApplet)
- [ ] Implement create(), render(), resize(), pause(), resume(), dispose()
- [ ] Map Processing lifecycle to LibGDX:
  - settings() → LwjglApplicationConfiguration
  - setup() → create()
  - draw() → render()
- [ ] LibGDXRenderer instantiated and used via RenderContext
- [ ] Main method uses Lwjgl3Application instead of PApplet.main()
- [ ] Application runs with LibGDX backend
- [ ] All subsystems still initialize correctly (UDP, Stage, Channel, etc.)
- [ ] Window size and properties match previous behavior
- [ ] Frame rate locked at 30fps (use Gdx.graphics.setForegroundFPS())
- [ ] Application exits cleanly with proper disposal

### Technical Notes
**Lifecycle Mapping**:
```java
// BEFORE (Processing)
public class TesseractMain extends PApplet {
    public void settings() {
        size(1400, 800, P3D);
        pixelDensity(displayDensity());
    }

    public void setup() {
        background(0);
        frameRate(30);
        // ... initialization
    }

    public void draw() {
        // ... render loop
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        PApplet.main("app.TesseractMain", args);
    }
}

// AFTER (LibGDX)
public class TesseractMain implements ApplicationListener {
    private IRenderer renderer;

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Lwjgl3ApplicationConfiguration config = new Lwjgl3ApplicationConfiguration();
        config.setTitle("Tesseract");
        config.setWindowedMode(1400, 800);
        config.setForegroundFPS(30);
        // Enable HDPI if available (macOS retina)
        config.useVsync(true);

        new Lwjgl3Application(new TesseractMain(), config);
    }

    @Override
    public void create() {
        renderer = new LibGDXRenderer();
        renderer.create(1400, 800);
        RenderContext.setRenderer(renderer);

        // All the setup() code here
        // ... initialization
    }

    @Override
    public void render() {
        // All the draw() code here
        if (!setupComplete) return;

        renderer.beginFrame();
        // ... business logic
        onScreen.draw();
        udpModel.send();
        renderer.endFrame();
    }

    @Override
    public void resize(int width, int height) {
        renderer.resize(width, height);
    }

    @Override
    public void pause() { }

    @Override
    public void resume() { }

    @Override
    public void dispose() {
        renderer.dispose();
        WebsocketInterface.get().shutdownServer();
    }
}
```

**Threading Consideration**:
- Remove the `thread("completeConfiguration")` hack - LibGDX doesn't have JOGL's threading issues
- Can initialize synchronously in create(), or use LibGDX's Timer/Task system if async needed

**Input Handling**:
- Need to set up Gdx.input.setInputProcessor() for mouse/keyboard
- Create InputProcessor implementation that delegates to onScreen

