## P1: Headless Renderer for Raspberry Pi

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Small (4-6 hours)
**Dependencies**: P0 Core Rendering Abstraction
**Spec Reference**: User requirements for headless mode on Pi
**Status Reference**: STATUS-libgdx-migration.md (Alternative approaches)

### Description
Create a no-op renderer for headless mode on Raspberry Pi where there's no display, only LED output via UDP. This allows the application to run without OpenGL or windowing system.

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Create `HeadlessRenderer implements IRenderer`
- [ ] All rendering methods are no-ops (do nothing)
- [ ] getFrameRate() returns configured frame rate (30)
- [ ] projectX/projectY perform math without OpenGL (camera matrix math)
- [ ] Can run application with HeadlessRenderer without crash
- [ ] LED output via UDP still works (business logic unaffected)
- [ ] Much lower CPU/memory usage than headed renderer
- [ ] Configuration option to select renderer mode (--headless flag)
- [ ] Unit tests: HeadlessRenderer doesn't require OpenGL context

### Technical Notes
**Renderer Selection**:
```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    boolean headless = Arrays.asList(args).contains("--headless");

    if (headless) {
        // No LibGDX application - just run business logic
        TesseractMain main = new TesseractMain();
        main.initHeadless();
        main.runHeadlessLoop();
    } else {
        // Normal LibGDX application
        Lwjgl3ApplicationConfiguration config = new Lwjgl3ApplicationConfiguration();
        // ... configure
        new Lwjgl3Application(new TesseractMain(), config);
    }
}
```

**HeadlessRenderer Implementation**:
```java
public class HeadlessRenderer implements IRenderer {
    private int width, height;
    private float frameRate = 30f;

    @Override
    public void create(int width, int height) {
        this.width = width;
        this.height = height;
    }

    @Override
    public void drawPoint(float x, float y, float z, int r, int g, int b) {
        // No-op
    }

    @Override
    public float projectX(float x, float y, float z) {
        // Simplified projection without OpenGL
        // Just return x as screen coordinate (good enough for LED mapping)
        return x + width / 2;
    }

    // ... all other methods are no-ops or simple stubs
}
```

**Coordinate Projection**:
- For LED mapping, screenX/screenY are used to map 3D points to 2D
- In headless mode, can use simplified projection (no actual rendering)
- May need basic matrix math for camera transforms
- Test LED mapping correctness with headless renderer

