## P2: Mouse and Keyboard Event Handling

**Status**: Not Started
**Effort**: Small (4-6 hours)
**Dependencies**: P1 Application Lifecycle Migration
**Spec Reference**: User requirements for interaction
**Status Reference**: STATUS-libgdx-migration.md (Event handling section)

### Description
Migrate mouse and keyboard event handling from Processing's callback methods to LibGDX's InputProcessor system.

### Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Create `TesseractInputProcessor implements InputProcessor`
- [ ] Handle mouse events (touchDown, touchUp, touchDragged)
- [ ] Handle keyboard events (keyDown, keyTyped)
- [ ] Delegate to OnScreen for mouse events
- [ ] Delegate to TesseractMain for keyboard events
- [ ] Map LibGDX input codes to Processing key codes if needed
- [ ] Mouse rotation still works (drag to rotate view)
- [ ] Keyboard shortcuts still work ('s' for sending, 'd' for drawing)
- [ ] Input handling works in both windowed and fullscreen modes

### Technical Notes
**InputProcessor Implementation**:
```java
public class TesseractInputProcessor implements InputProcessor {
    private TesseractMain main;
    private OnScreen onScreen;

    public TesseractInputProcessor(TesseractMain main, OnScreen onScreen) {
        this.main = main;
        this.onScreen = onScreen;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean touchDown(int screenX, int screenY, int pointer, int button) {
        onScreen.mousePressed(screenX, screenY);
        return true;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean touchUp(int screenX, int screenY, int pointer, int button) {
        onScreen.mouseReleased(screenX, screenY);
        return true;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean touchDragged(int screenX, int screenY, int pointer) {
        // Update mouse position for OnScreen
        return true;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean keyDown(int keycode) {
        // Map LibGDX keycode to character
        if (keycode == Input.Keys.S) {
            main.toggleSending();
        } else if (keycode == Input.Keys.D) {
            main.toggleDrawing();
        }
        return true;
    }

    // ... other InputProcessor methods
}
```

**Setup in TesseractMain**:
```java
@Override
public void create() {
    // ... renderer setup

    // Set up input handling
    TesseractInputProcessor inputProcessor = new TesseractInputProcessor(this, onScreen);
    Gdx.input.setInputProcessor(inputProcessor);
}
```

**Mouse Position**:
- Processing: `mouseX`, `mouseY` member variables
- LibGDX: `Gdx.input.getX()`, `Gdx.input.getY()`
- OnScreen needs access to current mouse position - store in renderer or pass as params

